     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">Hi all, I&#39;m starting with ggplot and I can&#39;t solve this\r\n(apparently simple) problem. I&#39;m using a sample of survey data (eph100) where P47T\r\nis individual income. The syntax<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">qplot(P47T, data = eph100,\r\ncolour=&quot;Red&quot;, binwidth=500)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">puts red borders, but</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">qplot(P47T, data = eph100,\r\ncolour=&quot;Blue&quot;, binwidth=500)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">does the same: red borders.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">When I want to fill the\r\nrectangles:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">qplot(P47T, data = eph100,\r\nfill=&quot;Blue&quot;, binwidth=500)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">The areas are filled with\r\nred!!</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">After reading answers to Ben’s\r\nquestion (superman emblem) I suppose this red is the default color for\r\nmisinterpretations.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">This syntax:</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">qplot(P47T, data = eph100,\r\ncolor=&quot;Green&quot;, fill=&quot;Blue&quot;, binwidth=500)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">returns a completely red histogram\r\n(borders and filling), with a legend that identifies the names of colors with different\r\ncolors. It seems that R is considering new objects called green and blue, but\r\nif I eliminate the quotation marks, results in an error, because R says: “object\r\n&#39;Green&#39; not found”<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">The numbers from the color\r\nchart neither work:</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">qplot(P47T, data = eph100, color=257, fill=490, binwidth=500)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">gives a completely blue\r\nhistogram, the same with any number combination.</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">Can anybody help?</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"left\" style=\"background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Thanks<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div>"
